PPA Source Package — fcitx5-skey
=================================

This directory contains the Debian packaging for fcitx5-skey, intended
for upload to Ubuntu Launchpad PPA.

Quick Start
-----------

1. Create the orig tarball (bundles skey-engine source):

    ./scripts/make-ppa-source.sh

2. Build the source package:

    debuild -S -sa

3. Check package quality:

    lintian --pedantic ../fcitx5-skey_*.changes

4. Upload to Launchpad PPA:

    dput ppa:collyn094/fcitx5-skey ../fcitx5-skey_*_source.changes

About skey-engine (Rust)
-------------------------

skey-engine is a stateless Vietnamese input method engine written in Rust.
It ships as a static library (libskey_engine.a) that links into the C++
fcitx5 addon.

The engine has zero external Cargo dependencies — it only uses the Rust
standard library. This makes it suitable for offline build environments
like Launchpad buildd.

During the build, CMake receives `-DSKEY_ENGINE_SOURCE_DIR=$(CURDIR)/skey-engine`
(via debian/rules) to use the bundled source instead of cloning from GitHub.
